# `core.autocrlf` is on for most people working on this repo, and Git decides
# what is binary by sniffing the first 8000 bytes for a NUL. That heuristic has
# never been wrong about a PNG — but a mangled icon is a silent failure that
# shows up as a broken square on someone else's machine, days later, and this
# repo has already lost an afternoon to a bad icon checkout. Say it outright.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
